# Phase 1 — Engine Reset + Sector 18 Vertical Slice — Implementation Plan

> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.

**Goal:** Replace the existing `src/game/game3d.ts` alpha with a layered, data-driven engine that ships Sector 18 at shipping grade on desktop + mobile, one AI rival, Spark Burst pickup, full race state machine, and the Phase 1 section of the §6.5 performance budget.

**Architecture:** Clean-room Three.js engine split into `engine/` (loop, input, audio, events, assets), `sim/` (renderer-agnostic physics, car, AI, pickups, race FSM, track-runtime), `render/` (Three scene, spline track mesh, instanced props, car mesh, HUD, FX), `ui/` (menus, overlays, mobile controls), `content/` (tracks, cars, pickups as JSON), `data/` (Zod schemas + IndexedDB), `worker/` (Cloudflare Worker scaffold, no endpoints yet in Phase 1), and `util/` (math). Old monolith `game3d.ts` and the dead 2D `game.ts` are deleted. Sim must never import Three; render reads sim snapshots but never mutates them.

**Tech Stack:** TypeScript 5, Three.js 0.184, Vite 7, Vitest 3, Zod 3, Playwright (added in this plan), Cloudflare Workers/Pages via Wrangler 4.

**Scope not in this plan (deferred to Phase 2+):** Aisle Nine, Driftwood Patio, Workshop Floor, Wing C. Rookie / Muscle / Pro cars. Pickups beyond Spark Burst. Time Trial / Battle Tag / Championship. Audio content. Lightmap bake (pipeline slot is ready; neutral placeholder texture ships in Phase 1). Ghost upload worker endpoints.

**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-23-rc-racer-uplift-design.plan`

---

## Task roadmap

| Group | Tasks | What lands |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 1–4 | Dependencies, new module skeleton, test harness, no behaviour change yet |
| 2 | 5–7 | Zod schemas for track / car / pickup |
| 3 | 8–9 | Util math with spline + curvature + closest-point |
| 4 | 10–13 | Engine: event bus, fixed-step loop, input reshape, audio scaffold |
| 5 | 14–19 | Sim: track-runtime, tire + chassis, car, race FSM, pickup, AI |
| 6 | 20–25 | Render: scene, track mesh, prop instancer, car mesh, FX, camera |
| 7 | 26–28 | UI: title menu, overlay state, mobile-controls migration |
| 8 | 29–30 | Content: Sector 18 track JSON, Boulevard car JSON, Spark Burst |
| 9 | 31–33 | App wiring, delete old code, production build green |
| 10 | 34–35 | Playwright E2E smoke + visual + perf |

Tasks MUST be executed in numerical order within a group. Between groups, a later group MAY start once its predecessor's tests are green — groups 6–8 overlap naturally once 1–5 are merged.

