## Self-review

**Spec coverage** (walked through the spec section by section):

- §2 Invariants — covered by the architecture (sim/render separation enforced by imports), the 800-line rule (every file ≤ 400 typical), Three.js retained, Cloudflare retained (`wrangler.toml` unchanged, worker scaffold at `src/worker/index.ts`). ✓
- §3 Success criteria — Phase 1 targets (#1 viewport-dominant, #6 bundle ≤180KB, #7 coverage ≥80%) are enforced by `index.html` + vite chunk config + vitest coverage threshold. Phase 1 does not attempt #2 (5 tracks), #3/#4 (multi-car perf under full roster), or #5 (championship) — those are Phase 2+. ✓
- §4 Module architecture — Task 2 stubs every module, later tasks fill them, Task 32 deletes the replaced files. ✓
- §5 Simulation — Tasks 15–19 implement physics, car, track-runtime, race FSM, pickups, AI. Stock class only; Rookie / Muscle / Pro deferred per §11.1. ✓
- §6 Rendering — Tasks 20–25 implement scene, track mesh, prop instancer, car mesh, camera, FX, HUD. Baked lightmap uses a neutral placeholder (Task 29) — the binding slot exists; real bake is Phase 2. ✓
- §7 Content model — Tasks 5–7 + 29–30 implement schemas and ship Sector 18 + Boulevard + Spark Burst. ✓
- §8 Audio — Task 13 ships the bus scaffold. Samples come in Phase 2. ✓
- §9 Persistence — Task 28 ships settings + best-lap localStorage. IndexedDB + CF KV come in Phase 2–3. ✓
- §10 Testing — Tasks 5, 7, 8–19, 21, 22, 28, 34, 35 cover unit / integration / E2E / visual / perf. Coverage threshold in vitest config (Task 1). Determinism test deferred to Phase 2 (requires stable input recording format, not needed until replay lands). ✓
