- §12 Anti-patterns — The architecture and file-size rules prevent monolithic regrowth; sim imports are guarded by convention and reviewed per task. ✓

**Placeholder scan:** No TBDs, TODOs, "similar to Task N", "handle edge cases", or vague "add appropriate X" instructions. Every code block is complete. Every test shows both the failing case (exported name missing) and the passing case.

**Type consistency:** `Vec3`, `InputFrame`, `CarRuntime`, `CarSnapshot`, `RaceState`, `RaceStatus`, `TrackRuntime`, `SplineControl`, `ProgressSample`, `SurfaceBand`, `PropId`, `CarTuning`, `PickupId`, `HudRefs` — all defined once, referenced consistently across tasks. Task 19's `aiInput` signature matches Task 27's caller. Task 15's `ProgressSample.t` is used in Task 19 (`previousT` arg) and Task 31 (`playerPrevT`/`rivalPrevT`).

**Scope check:** Each task is 2–5 minutes of focused work except Task 31 (`app.ts` wiring) which is ~15 minutes — acceptable because it is the single integration point that cannot be decomposed without duplicating context. Every task ends with a commit.

**One intentional deferment called out in the plan rather than hidden as a TODO:** Determinism test (spec §10) moves to Phase 2 because it requires a stable input-recording format that has no consumer in Phase 1. This is documented in Group 10's scope description and the §10 coverage note above.

